  "source_difference": "Only the two plain-profile configuration fragments changed between debug and plain verification; production/test code identical. Failed plain001 refused DEBUG_KERNEL=n because EXPERT selects it, before compilation. Retry002 retains explicit lockdep/debug-spin/list exclusions and BUG=y.",
  "scope": "Four q35/KVM SMP2 kernels: C/Rust debug and C/Rust nondebug; each passes39 combined (30core+9BRD), then30 isolated core. All14 completion and10 swait definitions selected exactly once; scheduler-text placement retained.",
  "initializer_coverage": "Final selflinks, working rawlock, IRQ-preserving initialization in enabled/disabled modes; static same/distinct caller key/name and LD_WAIT_SPIN under lockdep; nondebug null ignored arguments and explicit unavailable metadata.",
  "diagnostics": "No compiler/objtool or rejected runtime diagnostics; no required skips. BUG enabled in all four. Debug pair enables lockdep/raw-lock nesting/atomic-sleep/list checks; plain pair explicitly disables them.",
  "remaining_C": "Raw-lock/lockdep/list/state/LKMM adapters, completion inline initialization/reset, scheduler and generic consumer macros.",
  "limitations": "No full subsystem divergence, architecture expansion, module/performance or exhaustive race coverage. Exclusive initializer contract and external publication still required.",
